{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794426458,"nonce":"OTFpPKVw1C7AWRAomWUMbH17KOk=","title":"cn::button leaves 3 signals behind per build","message":"Found while checking that rebuilding a form page does not add signals (fs-components v0.0.7 work). Counting live signals around a build of one widget:\n- `div`: 0 left behind\n- `text_input`: 0 left behind\n- `cn::button`: 3 left behind per build\n\nRepro: build a tree containing one `cn::button`, drop it, build again; repeat. The signal count rises by 3 each round with a button and stays flat without it. Dropping the built tree does not release them.\n\nThis is an older defect of its own, separate from signals owned by the caller (see the closed \"Signals and deriveds can never be disposed\", which is the missing disposal path in general). It adds up for pages that are rebuilt often.\n\nEffect downstream: the form rebuild test in fs-components (crates/fs-admin-frontend/tests/slot_rebuild.rs) cannot count signals over the whole page, because every button would add to the count; the comment there refers to this. The field data leak is counted separately in the fields crate.\n\nTo find: which three signals `cn::button` creates per build (label, state, and what else) and why they are not released with the built tree.","files":null}]}